{%- comment -%} ===================== Every setting ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-reference-settings" data-group="Reference" data-title="Every setting" data-time="8 min"
  data-keywords="settings table ranges defaults speed smoothing y scale fine aim deadzone update rate dpi sync to game activate deactivate">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Reference</p>
    <h1>Every setting</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Each setting's range, default and when to change it, in one place.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">8 min</span></div>
  </header>
  <p>Change one setting at a time, then test it in a training area. "Start here" is a safe first value.</p>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-settings--aim">
    <h2>Mouse aim</h2>
    <p>Where: HOME › <b>Settings</b> › <b>Aim</b>. Hip aim and ADS aim each have their own Speed and Smoothing.</p>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings">
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--speed"><td><b>Speed</b> (Hip aim)</td><td data-label="What it does">How fast your view turns. The app shows the matching cm/360 under it.</td><td data-label="Range">Standard (0) to 100, step 1. Higher is faster.</td><td data-label="Default">Set by your game</td><td data-label="Start here">The default</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">turning feels slow</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">you overshoot targets</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--ads-speed"><td><b>Speed</b> (ADS aim)</td><td data-label="What it does">Turn speed while aiming down sights.</td><td data-label="Range">Same as hip, or 0 to 100</td><td data-label="Default">Same as hip</td><td data-label="Start here">Same as hip</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">ADS feels slow</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">ADS feels twitchy</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--smoothing"><td><b>Smoothing</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Evens out small bumps in your aim.</td><td data-label="Range">Disabled, Light, Balanced, Heavy, Custom</td><td data-label="Default">Disabled</td><td data-label="Start here">Disabled</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">aim looks jittery</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">aim feels floaty</td></tr>
        <tr class="m2-group-row"><td colspan="7">Custom smoothing, Standard</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--precision"><td><b>Precision</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Smoother at low speeds, a heavier reticle. 0 switches this filter off.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">0 %</td><td data-label="Start here">0 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">slow tracking is shaky</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">aim feels heavy</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--response"><td><b>Response</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How quickly the filter follows you. Needs Precision above 0.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">10 %</td><td data-label="Start here">10 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">aim lags behind you</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">aim is still shaky</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--easing"><td><b>Easing</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How gently the filter blends in. Needs Precision above 0.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">35 %</td><td data-label="Start here">35 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">the change feels sudden</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">aim feels soft</td></tr>
        <tr class="m2-group-row"><td colspan="7">Custom smoothing, Classic</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--smooth"><td><b>Smooth</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How much smoothing. Higher means more.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">0</td><td data-label="Start here">0</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">aim looks jittery</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">aim feels floaty</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--decay"><td><b>Decay</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How much Smooth leans on past movement.</td><td data-label="Range">0–20, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">9 (the app's "usual")</td><td data-label="Start here">9</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">aim feels floaty</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">aim feels jittery</td></tr>
        <tr class="m2-group-row"><td colspan="7">ADS Activation</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--activate"><td><b>Activate</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Keeps hip settings this long after you start aiming, while the game zooms in.</td><td data-label="Range">0–1000 ms, step 4</td><td data-label="Default">0 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">0 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">aim jumps as you zoom in</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">the switch feels late</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--deactivate"><td><b>Deactivate</b></td><td data-label="What it does">The same, when you stop aiming.</td><td data-label="Range">0–1000 ms, step 4</td><td data-label="Default">0 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">0 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">aim jumps as you zoom out</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">the switch back feels late</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--smooth-ads"><td><b>Smooth ADS Transition</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Blends from hip to ADS settings instead of switching at once.</td><td data-label="Range">On or off</td><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td data-label="Start here">Off</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">turn it on if the switch feels sudden</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">turn it off if it feels slow</td></tr>
        <tr class="m2-group-row"><td colspan="7">Advanced</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--fine-aim"><td><b>Fine aim</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Makes small, slow moves count for more. Flicks stay the same.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 5 (0 = off)</td><td data-label="Default">0 %</td><td data-label="Start here">0 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">small corrections feel stuck</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">small moves feel jumpy</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--y-scale"><td><b>Y Scale</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Up-and-down speed compared with left-and-right.</td><td data-label="Range">30–200 %, step 5</td><td data-label="Default">100 %</td><td data-label="Start here">100 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">looking up and down feels slow</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">vertical aim overshoots</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--ignore-tiny"><td><b>Ignore tiny movement</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Hand movement slower than this is ignored.</td><td data-label="Range">0–300 mm/s, step 1 (0 = off)</td><td data-label="Default">0 (off)</td><td data-label="Start here">0</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">a resting hand still moves the view</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">small moves are ignored</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--feel"><td><b>Feel</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How your aim stops when your hand stops.</td><td data-label="Range">Snappy, Balanced, Smooth</td><td data-label="Default">Snappy</td><td data-label="Start here">Snappy (the app's pick)</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">try Smooth if stops feel abrupt</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">go back to Snappy if aim drifts</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--startup-feel"><td><b>Start-up feel</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How gently a move starts after your hand was still.</td><td data-label="Range">0–200 ms, step 5 (0 = instant)</td><td data-label="Default">0 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">0 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">starts feel twitchy</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">starts feel slow</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-settings--sticks">
    <h2>Controller sticks</h2>
    <p>Where: HOME › <b>Settings</b> › <b>Aim</b> › <b>Switch ›</b> (Controller).</p>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings">
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--stick-sensitivity"><td><b>Sensitivity</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How far the stick turns your view.</td><td data-label="Range">10–100 %</td><td data-label="Default">The app default</td><td data-label="Start here">The default</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">turning feels slow</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">you overshoot</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--inner"><td><b>Inner</b> deadzone</td><td data-label="What it does">Ignores stick movement near the centre.</td><td data-label="Range">0–40 %</td><td data-label="Default">8 %</td><td data-label="Start here">8 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">the stick drifts</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">small moves are ignored</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--outer"><td><b>Outer</b> deadzone</td><td data-label="What it does">Reaches full speed before the stick hits the edge.</td><td data-label="Range">0–40 %</td><td data-label="Default">0 %</td><td data-label="Start here">0 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">you can't reach full speed</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">full speed comes too early</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--anti"><td><b>Anti</b> (anti-deadzone)</td><td data-label="What it does">Steps over the game's own deadzone, so small moves count.</td><td data-label="Range">0–40 %</td><td data-label="Default">The app default</td><td data-label="Start here">Match the game's deadzone</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">small moves do nothing</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">the view creeps on its own</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--limit"><td><b>Limit</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Caps how far the sticks can go.</td><td data-label="Range">10–100 %</td><td data-label="Default">100 %</td><td data-label="Start here">100 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">turning tops out too soon</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">you want a lower top speed</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--deadzone-shape"><td><b>Deadzone shape</b></td><td data-label="What it does">One round deadzone, or one per direction.</td><td data-label="Range">Round, Per-axis</td><td data-label="Default">The app default</td><td data-label="Start here">Round</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">try Per-axis for straight-line aim</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">go back to Round if diagonals feel off</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-settings--device">
    <h2>Device and Translation</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings">
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--update-rate"><td><b>Update Rate</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How often the EXO updates the console.</td><td data-label="Range">125, 250, 500, 1000 Hz</td><td data-label="Default">1000 Hz on mouse configs.</td><td data-label="Start here">The default</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">aim feels a little behind</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">support asks you to test it</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--mouse-dpi"><td><b>Mouse DPI</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Tells the EXO your mouse's DPI, so Speed means the same on any mouse.</td><td data-label="Range">Your mouse's DPI. The app recommends 3200–12000.</td><td data-label="Default">Measured or typed in</td><td data-label="Start here">3200</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">match your mouse; don't use it to change speed</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">match your mouse; use Speed instead</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--connection-method"><td><b>Connection Method</b></td><td data-label="What it does">The console this config plays on.</td><td data-label="Range">PlayStation 5, Xbox, PC</td><td data-label="Default">Picked in New config</td><td data-label="Start here">Your console</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--what-you-play-with"><td><b>What you play with</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Which kind of controls this config expects.</td><td data-label="Range">Auto, Mouse + Keyboard, Controller, Joystick + Mouse</td><td data-label="Default">Auto</td><td data-label="Start here">Auto</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--sync-to-game"><td><b>Sync to game</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Sends aim in step with your game's frame rate.</td><td data-label="Range">60, 120, Custom (20–360 Hz), Off</td><td data-label="Default">60</td><td data-label="Start here">The frame rate you play at</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">your game runs at 120 fps</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">your game runs at 60 fps</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-settings--global">
    <h2>Global Settings</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings">
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr id="p-reference-settings--passthrough-shortcut"><td><b>Pass-through</b> shortcut</td><td data-label="What it does">Pauses your config for menus, chat and typing.</td><td data-label="Range">Any key combo</td><td data-label="Default"><span class="m2-key">1</span> + <span class="m2-key">5</span></td></tr>
