</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Glossary ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-reference-glossary" data-group="Reference" data-title="Glossary" data-time="5 min"
  data-keywords="glossary words meaning definition what does mean cm/360 dpi ads hip deadzone">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Reference</p>
    <h1>Glossary</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Plain meanings for the words you'll see in the app and this manual.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="m2-time">5 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-glossary--aim">
    <h2>Aim words</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Word</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--ads"><td><b>ADS</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">Aim down sights: when you zoom in to aim. The opposite is hip fire.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--anti-deadzone"><td><b>Anti-deadzone</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">A push past the game's deadzone, so tiny moves still turn your view.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--cm360"><td><b>cm/360</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">How far you move your mouse, in centimetres, to turn all the way around. Lower means faster.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--curve"><td><b>Curve</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">How turn speed grows as you move faster.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--deadzone"><td><b>Deadzone</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">A small area around the stick's centre where movement is ignored.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--dpi"><td><b>DPI</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">How many dots your mouse reports per inch of movement.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--hip"><td><b>Hip fire</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">Aiming and shooting without zooming in.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--polling-rate"><td><b>Polling rate</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">How many times a second your mouse reports, in Hz. 1000 Hz is common.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--smoothing"><td><b>Smoothing</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">Evens out small bumps in your aim. Too much feels floaty.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--sync"><td><b>Sync to game</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">Sends aim in step with your game's frame rate.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-glossary--exo">
    <h2>EXO and app words</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Word</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--ai-scripts"><td><b>AI Scripts</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">The app's screen for Scripts that switch on by themselves for the gun you hold (automatic gun detection).</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--anti-recoil-lab"><td><b>Anti-Recoil Lab</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">The tool that builds anti-recoil for a gun.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--auth"><td><b>AUTH</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">The back port for the PS5 auth dongle, or your own genuine Xbox controller.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--config"><td><b>Config</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">Everything for one way of playing: game, console, aim, mappings and Scripts.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--connection-method"><td><b>Connection Method</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">The console a config plays on.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--hdmi-loop"><td><b>HDMI loop</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">Console into HDMI IN, HDMI OUT to the TV, so the EXO can see the game.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--mappings"><td><b>Mappings</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">What each button, key or click sends to the console.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--native-mk"><td><b>Native Mouse &amp; Keyboard</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">A config type for PC players, in final testing.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--passthrough"><td><b>Pass-through</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">A shortcut that pauses your config for menus, chat and typing.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--script"><td><b>Script</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">A trigger plus steps the EXO presses for you, like rapid fire.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--tournament-mode"><td><b>Tournament Mode</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">One switch that turns every Script off.</td></tr>
        <tr id="p-reference-glossary--update-rate"><td><b>Update Rate</b></td><td data-label="Meaning">How often the EXO updates the console, in Hz.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>
</article>

