{%- comment -%} ===================== Fair play ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-reference-fair-play" data-group="Reference" data-title="Fair play and Tournament Mode" data-time="2 min"
  data-keywords="fair play rules tournament mode events esports scripts off">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Reference</p>
    <h1>Fair play and Tournament Mode</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Play by the rules, and switch every Script off in one tap when you need to.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="m2-time">2 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-fair-play--rules">
    <h2>Follow the rules</h2>
    <p class="m2-lead">Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-fair-play--tournament-mode">
    <h2>1. Turn on Tournament Mode</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On HOME, tap <b>⋮</b>, then <b>Global Settings</b>.</li>
      <li>On the <b>General</b> tab, switch on <b>Tournament Mode</b> (1).</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="m2-table"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Turns off</th><th>Keeps</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td data-label="Turns off">Scripts, rapid fire, anti-recoil help and gun-detection actions</td><td data-label="Keeps">Your mappings, stick settings and aim settings</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-gl-tournament.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="432" loading="lazy"
        alt="Global Settings, General tab. 1: the Tournament Mode switch, on.">
      <figcaption>Figure FAIR-PLAY.1 — Global Settings › General › Tournament Mode, switched on</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Tournament Mode</b></td><td>One switch turns off every Script, turbo and AI action. Remaps and stick settings stay.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-gl-tournament-chip.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="427" loading="lazy"
        alt="HOME while Tournament Mode is on: a Tournament chip under the config name, BO2 Ranked.">
      <figcaption>Figure FAIR-PLAY.2 — HOME shows the Tournament chip</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-fair-play--check">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul><li><b>App:</b> HOME shows a Tournament chip.</li><li><b>Game:</b> your Scripts no longer fire.</li></ul>
      <p>A Script still runs? <a href="#p-help-scripts--script-wont-stop">A Script won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Safety and care ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-reference-safety" data-group="Reference" data-title="Safety and care" data-time="2 min"
  data-keywords="safety care clean heat vents water warranty">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Reference</p>
    <h1>Safety and care</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Keep your EXO working well for years.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="m2-time">2 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-safety--use">
    <h2>Everyday use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep the vents on the case clear. Don't cover the EXO or stack things on it while it's on.</li>
      <li>Keep it dry. Don't use it near water or spilled drinks.</li>
      <li>Use good USB and HDMI cables, and pull them out by the plug, not the cord.</li>
      <li>Use a normal USB charger or PC USB port for AUX/POWER.</li>
      <li>Keep small parts, like the PS5 auth dongle, away from small children.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-reference-safety--clean">
    <h2>Cleaning</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Unplug the EXO first.</li>
      <li>Wipe it with a soft, dry cloth.</li>
      <li>Don't use sprays, solvents or water.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>

